IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `oas-core`
IMPORT `oas-core-measures`
IMPORT `oa1-part1-waiver`

-- Tests of oa1-part1-waiver (s 5(4) to (8)). Every person here was born on October 1, 1961, so every day the Act fixes
-- ("the day on which the person attains 65 years of age") is October 1, 2026; the days before it end on September 30, 2026.

§ `s 5(4): the Minister may waive`

-- The Minister may waive "on the day on which a person attains 65 years of age", if satisfied (lines 134-135).
#ASSERT `s 5(4): the Minister may waive the requirement for an application` (YMD 1961 10 1) (YMD 2026 10 1) TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`s 5(4): the Minister may waive the requirement for an application` (YMD 1961 10 1) (YMD 2026 9 30) TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 5(4): the Minister may waive the requirement for an application` (YMD 1961 10 1) (YMD 2026 10 2) TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 5(4): the Minister may waive the requirement for an application` (YMD 1961 10 1) (YMD 2026 10 1) FALSE)

§ `s 5(5): notice of intent`

#ASSERT `s 5(5): the person is owed written notice of the intention to waive, with the information on which the Minister intends to rely` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`s 5(5): the person is owed written notice of the intention to waive, with the information on which the Minister intends to rely` FALSE)

§ `s 5(6): inaccuracies`

-- "before the day on which they attain 65 years of age": the last day to file is September 30, 2026.
#ASSERT `s 5(6): the last day on which the person may file the statement correcting inaccuracies` (YMD 1961 10 1) EQUALS (YMD 2026 9 30)
-- No inaccuracy, nothing to file: complied. Inaccuracy corrected on the last day: complied. On the 65th birthday: not.
#ASSERT `s 5(6): the person has complied` (YMD 1961 10 1) FALSE FALSE (YMD 2026 9 1)
#ASSERT `s 5(6): the person has complied` (YMD 1961 10 1) TRUE TRUE (YMD 2026 9 30)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 5(6): the person has complied` (YMD 1961 10 1) TRUE TRUE (YMD 2026 10 1))
#ASSERT NOT (`s 5(6): the person has complied` (YMD 1961 10 1) TRUE FALSE (YMD 2026 9 1))

§ `s 5(7): declining the waiver`

#ASSERT `s 5(7): the person has declined the waiver` (YMD 1961 10 1) TRUE (YMD 2026 9 30)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 5(7): the person has declined the waiver` (YMD 1961 10 1) TRUE (YMD 2026 10 1))
#ASSERT NOT (`s 5(7): the person has declined the waiver` (YMD 1961 10 1) FALSE (YMD 2026 9 30))

§ `s 5(8): cancellation of the waiver`

-- The Minister must intend the waiver, require an application before the 65th birthday, and notify the person in writing.
#ASSERT `s 5(8): the person is required to make an application` (YMD 1961 10 1) TRUE TRUE (YMD 2026 9 30) TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`s 5(8): the person is required to make an application` (YMD 1961 10 1) TRUE TRUE (YMD 2026 10 1) TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 5(8): the person is required to make an application` (YMD 1961 10 1) TRUE TRUE (YMD 2026 9 30) FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 5(8): the person is required to make an application` (YMD 1961 10 1) FALSE TRUE (YMD 2026 9 30) TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 5(8): the person is required to make an application` (YMD 1961 10 1) TRUE FALSE (YMD 2026 9 30) TRUE)

§ `The waiver as a whole`

-- Waived: made, not declined, not cancelled. Declined or cancelled: not waived.
#ASSERT `s 5(4): the requirement for an application is waived` TRUE FALSE FALSE
#ASSERT NOT (`s 5(4): the requirement for an application is waived` TRUE TRUE FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 5(4): the requirement for an application is waived` TRUE FALSE TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 5(4): the requirement for an application is waived` FALSE FALSE FALSE)
